hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1610","Narrated to us Bundar — Muhammad ibn Bashshar — on the authority of Ibn Abi 'Adi — from Sa'id — from Qatadah — from Anas ibn Malik (RA) that the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) said:

*""Indeed, I enter into the prayer and intend to prolong it, but then I hear the crying of a child. So I shorten my prayer, knowing the distress of the child’s mother due to his crying.""*

**CHAPTER:**"
